WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.320
Tokyo is a target.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.050
Even with the Logos threat gone,

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.730
crimes involving Willwear misuse still occur,

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.160
and are escalating by the day.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.410
And to make matters worse,

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.740
the quicksand zone is now the perfect 
hiding place for illegal immigrants.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.110
Tokyo... no, our entire country

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.530
has been left far too undefended until now.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.010
You haven't changed, Inagi-san.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:26.620
I'm grateful.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.920
Having the governor's direct support

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.380
has enabled us to make development 
of these enhancement units a reality.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.480
How did you deceive the Diet?

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.120
"Deceived" is putting it so crudely...

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.130
How did you—

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.740
Right, whatever. Let's start the test.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.780
Wait a second...

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.830
I'm doing final checks now.

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.030
Sure, sure.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.480
Well, it's thanks to Inagi-san that Unit 8 has 
a lot more freedom to act than before.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:57.700
We're grateful.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.880
What's with that laugh? It's creepy!

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.090
You've sure grown up, huh?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.760
What are you doing? You're the governor!

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.550
Stop laughing!

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:16.870
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.420
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.350
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:29.690
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.020
<b>File 2: Endless Avenger</b>

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.110
The hit-and-run driver is on Yokosuka Bridge, 
fleeing toward the Bahori Coast.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.960
An incident in Kanagawa?

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.280
But...

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.080
We're about to start the test.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.520
If you have complaints, tell Funasaka-san.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.290
Forget this and head to the scene.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:31.100
<b>Otsuka</b>

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.100
<b>Kanagawa</b>

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.090
This is Oscar II, heading out first!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.750
I'm too late?

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.000
What's that?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.790
This is the seventh incident.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.710
The culprit is committing crimes 
to draw out the police.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.930
It seems safe to assume that.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.860
And here's the footage we have of them.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.890
What's this Willwear?

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.350
Is that a Centaur Unit?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.410
A Centa... What?

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.190
I'll explain.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.690
The Willwear is an off-the-shelf, 
all-purpose model.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.110
But what makes this one special 
is this part, the Centaur Unit.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.500
By combining, it can bring out 
the Willwear's full power,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.790
vastly increasing its maneuverability.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.900
It has a spare battery,

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.590
so you can use it over a long period of time.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:37.290
In the future, we hope it can be used

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.080
to develop remote areas or for rescue 
operations in disaster zones.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.130
The Polska police originally

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:49.050
developed this unit to enable the 
formation of a Willwear cavalry.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.800
In Poland?

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.310
Seeing it used for crime this way 
is extremely disappointing.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.770
Is the criminal someone who has 
something against Poland?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.360
Or against the police?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.280
Our only clue is this mark left at the scene.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:08.130
It may be some kind of message, since it's 
left behind at every crime scene.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.210
<b>To Director Kazama 
Confidential</b>

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.930
Hey, this envelope—

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.400
<i>Hi, hi! I figured it out!</i>

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.600
<i>I bet this is what the mark is!</i>

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.900
I see... It's the Aster Electrical 
Engineering company badge?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.260
What's a company badge?

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.770
Is it like a company logo?

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.860
That's right. Ours is...

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.370
This.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.460
Of all things, it's the company 
involved in that incident?

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:54.290
Incident?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.730
It was about eight years ago.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.190
This company manufactures 
precision Willwear parts,

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:04.300
but it was also involved in the illegal 
export of devices that could be

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.720
converted into weapons of mass destruction.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.040
The media reported

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.470
that some of the top brass on the 
police force may have known,

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.880
but covered it up in return for bribes.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.060
Huh...

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:17.850
"Huh," nothing.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.850
You need to know this, right?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.790
The police firmly denied it, of course.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:28.340
But during the frenzy over the incident, 
a police officer resigned.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.700
A voluntary resignation, ostensibly.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:34.660
<b>Name: Raidou Tetsuo 

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.350
Sergeant Raidou Tetsuo.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:34.660
He was 45 years old.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.700
He voluntarily resigned?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:37.700
Yes.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.660
Naturally, the media wasn't satisfied with that.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:44.380
They thought he was just being 
used as a scapegoat.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.320
If that's true,

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.470
it would give him plenty of 
reason to hate the police.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.570
Sounds like another big mess.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.640
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.110
Yes, this is Unit 8.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.280
What?

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.180
The driver is only slightly injured.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.940
If it's Raidou who did this,

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.080
and he kidnapped the director,

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.390
does that mean the director 
was involved in the case?

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:12.780
I couldn't say for sure...

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.580
This is Yamabuki.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.040
After leaving the police force, Raidou went

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.300
through several jobs and addresses.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.670
He disappeared from his last known address, 
a Nerima apartment, last year.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:29.010
Asami knows Director Kazama pretty well, right?

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.410
That's the one who took 
advantage of Kazari-kun.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.640
Would he tell her anything private?

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.100
So I mean...

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.270
Is there anyone who hated the director?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.060
She seems to be in a good mood.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.030
Yes, this is Yamabuki.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.100
Boss,

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.650
Raidou is still missing,

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:01.250
but I found a storage warehouse 
rented in his name.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.120
A rented warehouse?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.440
Good work, Polish policewoman!

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.050
Asami, that's enough.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.330
You can buy us some bean mochi as a gift.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.200
Bye.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.550
Emilia-chan, you be ready to go, too.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.880
Me, too?

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.360
Yes. Isn't Kyoukai-kun with you?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:20.390
Be ready.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:25.180
Hey, Kuroki-san...

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:25.850
Huh?

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:28.860
Vitals, all green.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:29.440
Lock.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:38.780
Inner unit, begin output.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.750
Oscar VII, set Foundation Omega Unit.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.510
It's been a long time, Inspector Kazama.

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:04.060
Or should I say "Director" now?

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.690
Who are you?

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.820
You were right. I was a failure as an officer.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:11.030
But why only me?

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:16.170
Why do the police still employ the others, 
and why do they still get promotions?

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:17.800
Are you Raidou?

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.200
That's right. I'm Raidou.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.620
The man you forced into 
retirement ten years ago.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:28.960
Well?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.540
I-I'm not really seeing anything.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:33.550
Go around to the back. Break in on my signal.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:36.860
What's wrong?

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.580
A-All right.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.980
Raidou, I swear I had nothing 
to do with that case.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:44.890
Believe me!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:45.520
Shut up!

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:48.980
Don't move, Raidou!

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.280
Unit 8?

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.090
Purge your Willwear!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.570
Slowly.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.490
That's right. Don't try anything funny.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.000
No!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.920
What are you doing, Oscar VII?!

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.420
Oscar VII, the director!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.380
R-Right!

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.610
Damn it, give it up already!

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.730
Take this!

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:46.250
K-Kyoukai-san!

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:48.730
What? The Falcon Unit?

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:50.620
Fire it now!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.880
It's not tested yet—

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.140
I'll test it during the fight!

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.220
Oh, fine...

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:24.410
There it is!

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.340
Okay!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:10.920
Permission to use burst mode!

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:11.710
Permission confirmed.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:12.740
Permission confirmed!

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:13.830
Permission confirmed!

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.510
Destructive Ram Cannon,

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:33.560
fire!

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:39.570
Splendid!

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.570
I got nearly all the data I needed at once!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.510
It's not him.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.490
This is not Raidou.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:51.950
What?!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.750
A memory transfer?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.720
How bold.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:59.490
Memory-transfer experimentation 
was an actual field of research at

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.750
the National Defense Academy, 
where I studied.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:04.050
Not the National Defense Medical College?

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.440
It was a type of brain-machine 
interface research.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:08.460
I see.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.850
In other words, this Asanuma guy

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.270
we captured had Raidou's memories implanted.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:17.360
I asked the chief to have them scan 
Asanuma's brain, and they found

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.980
that his hippocampus was particularly enlarged.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.070
His hippocampus?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.610
The same thing was seen in test subjects 
in the Academy's experiments.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:29.790
Of course, that research was shut 
down before it was completed,

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.050
and the school fired the professor responsible.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.040
I think his name was Doctor Mashirao...

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.500
Doctor Mashirao?

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.210
I'll go talk to the Academy.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:41.580
I'll hit Asanuma's apartment.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.550
That's Funabashi's jurisdiction, right?

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:44.730
Kuroki-kun!

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:47.890
Can I talk to you?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:02.900
Yo.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.290
Inspector Kuroki...

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.450
You know, you don't have to live on 
the same floor that Unit 8's on.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.300
I can easily get to the scene from here.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.500
It's about the man we captured.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.430
There's a chance his memories were implanted.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.600
Um, Inspector Kuroki, I actually—

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.830
Ow.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.710
Were you injured in the battle 
with the Centaur Unit?

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.140
No, no.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:29.960
I got this in a fight when I was a kid.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:30.980
A fight?

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:35.970
Yeah, thanks to a certain nosy bastard, 
I got off with nothing worse,

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.660
but it still hurts sometimes.

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.130
Since you have a strong sense of justice,

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.520
I'd guess you were protecting 
something, weren't you?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:43.800
Couldn't say.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.500
But ever since, I've been trying to do what I can,

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.940
one thing at a time, no matter how small it is.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:53.690
You know, I actually couldn't do 
subtraction until high school.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.120
Really?

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.150
After that, I started studying one thing at a time.

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.790
At the time, I hated it,

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.470
but now I'm proud of the effort I put in.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.880
Don't tell anyone what I just said.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.430
Especially Sena. Okay?

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.710
"Hiring part-timers for clinical trials.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:31.360
<b>Hiring 

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:31.360
Must be male, under the age of 30"?

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.320
Excuse me, I saw the ad for part-timers...

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:38.900
We're not hiring anymore. Go home.

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.250
Wait! At least hear me out!

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:46.420
I guess it won't be that easy to get in.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.220
Raidou...

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:04.520
This is Kuroki.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:07.250
Where the hell have you been, 
when you should be filing reports?

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:11.820
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:08.760
I have bigger problems!

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.800
I've found a man I believe to be Raidou.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:11.820
The location is—

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:15.560
Kuroki?

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.430
Hey, what's wrong?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.830
This is a good spot.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.040
People keep falling into the trap.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.880
Jeez, why does he go off on his own?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.630
I wish he would have taken me.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.130
Where's Funasaka-san?

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.130
He says he'll catch up later.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.390
Wait!

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.600
Give me permission to go.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.130
Permission granted.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:40.100
Kyoukai-kun?

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.850
His signal's been completely lost.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.560
The best I can do is narrow it to this area.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.770
Deploying drones to that area.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.600
Local police are searching, too.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:55.780
Emilia?

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:56.750
Yeah.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.840
I didn't know this,

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:02.310
but Emilia was evidently involved 
in testing the Centaur Unit.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:07.500
But her Willwear suddenly 
shut down during a mission.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.960
For three days, she was unable to move, 
trapped in a pitch-black Willwear.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.970
She had to wait three days for help to arrive.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.380
Three days?!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:20.500
Had it been a normal battery, it could've 
been purged, and all would've been fine.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:25.340
Emilia was a talented officer, but she 
started avoiding Willwear missions,

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.920
so there wasn't much place 
for her in the Polish police.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:31.770
That's why they sent her to us, I guess.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.310
Raidou!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:47.530
The body rots...

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:51.550
But my hatred will remain in this world,

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:56.300
to wreak vengeance on you police.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:01.730
I decided to let you help with 
the experiment, after all.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.300
Experiment?!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.830
When you next wake up,

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.440
you'll be a different person.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.820
You'll be him.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.860
Nothing on video?

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.660
What about you, Kyoukai-san?

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:27.310
Drones are picking up the voices,

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.120
so the quality isn't that good.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.260
Are you Doctor Mashirao?!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.550
Got it!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.760
Memories associated with strong emotion

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.970
have produced more experimental success.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:45.310
Which makes Raidou the perfect subject.

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.900
But there are compatibility 
issues to account for.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:54.110
I had to periodically rewrite 
Asanuma's memories.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.190
I wonder how compatible you are...

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.990
Kyoukai-kun, calculate a trajectory.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.190
You plan on charging straight in?

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:03.820
Yes.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:07.080
If we don't stop him, Raidou's memory 
will overwrite Kuroki-kun's!

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.000
But to do so, we'll have to 
break through obstacles.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.420
Your Wear can't handle that.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.460
Then I'll go.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.720
Yours is no different. We have 
to wait for Funasaka-san—

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.220
There's no time.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.300
Chief, I'll go.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.040
But I don't think this mission 
was in your contract...

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.560
There's no time for that!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:26.610
Boss!

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.100
Here we go.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.110
Stop it!

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.700
Don't resist. Accept it!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.100
It will all be over soon!

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:51.710
Wh-What?

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.610
Wh-Where is Inspector Kuroki?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.940
S-State your name and rank...

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:14.200
Your name!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:15.530
Don't talk to me that way!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.150
Kuroki Takeru, Superintendent General 
of the Metropolitan Police!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.570
I'm sorry.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.200
I was j-joking!

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.930
Inspector! I'm an inspector!

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.080
I'm so glad...

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:28.350
Get me out of this already.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:28.990
Right!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.150
You saved me.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.720
Thanks. I owe you one.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.140
And...

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.590
You did great.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.290
I have a long way to go.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.340
One thing at a time.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.760
Just one at a time.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.580
Right!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:09.380
The local police said Raidou's cause 
of death was heart disease.

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:11.940
Apparently, overuse of drugs

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:14.140
tore his body apart.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:16.940
From Doctor Mashirao's experiments?

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.220
Perhaps.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.570
The other surprising thing

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:23.680
was that Doctor Mashirao died two years ago.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.550
Then who was that man?

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:29.400
The body belonged to a man named 
Shirane, Mashirao's assistant.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.870
Doctor Mashirao knew he would die soon,

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:35.220
so he transferred his 
memories into his assistant.

00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:38.810
As with Asanuma, Shirane overwrote 
his memory several times,

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:42.560
and his hippocampus was quite enlarged.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:45.260
But there are still questions.

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:48.820
Like where he got the Centaur Unit...

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.830
Jeez, I don't even know who's who now!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:51.990
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.070
Ohakonyabachininko.

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:53.880
Huh? Is that Inagi-kun?

00:23:52.320 --> 00:24:04.870
File 3: Angel and God of Destruction

00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:57.550
Yes, but I ran risk management in case 
of this happening, so don't worry.

00:23:57.550 --> 00:23:58.790
That's the governor for you!

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:01.910
More importantly, next time, 
Unit 8 is in grave danger.

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:02.860
Be careful.

00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:04.390
Yeah, thanks.
